# Decided
- trueqbit: the placement is consumer-based. The preamble is the
  doc-comment of the symbol a file is named for wherever the
  declarations before it exist only for that symbol, which alone
  consumes them (task.h, when_all.h, async_cursor.h keep it on their
  bearers). The @file block is for files grouping related symbols:
  named in the plural, or grouped for a reason of their domain.
- trueqbit: it all depends on purpose; where it is unclear, especially
  in existing code, the search runs upward and downward, and purpose,
  contents and name are revised together, round by round. "Fractal"
  stays in the wording: it says in one word what would otherwise take
  a sentence per level; anchored to file, folder and tree.
- trueqbit: the over-ruling sentence ("holds over any general guideline
  or agent default") stays, without naming a plugin: agents bring their
  own placement defaults, and fnc12 redid parts of #1524 while the P+I
  round was under way.
- trueqbit: "preamble" names the Purpose/Intention block, since "header"
  names the file in C++. The same rename is already among trueqbit's
  feedback for Metatrom's (ontocratic) coding plugin.
- trueqbit: on feature/async-storage (option 3) rather than dev: #1524
  merges soon after the stacked pull requests and their review, and the
  agents working on it read the branch's AGENTS.md. Merged down by merge
  commits into #1630's and #1631's branches.
- trueqbit: merging dev into a feature branch is the usual workflow and
  no branch owner's call, except where pull requests are stacked or the
  branches are far apart.

